{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.617, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 21, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:42.686Z", "t_ms": 7613, "delta": "### Structure of a Mixture-of-Agents (MoA) Layer\n\n*"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.773, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 22, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:42.842Z", "t_ms": 7768, "delta": " **Layer Composition:** An MoA architecture consists of $l$ layers, where each layer $i$ contains $n$ full-"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.01, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 23, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:43.079Z", "t_ms": 8006, "delta": "fledged Large Language Models (LLMs), denoted as $A_{i,1}, A_{i,2}, \\dots,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.093, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 24, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:43.162Z", "t_ms": 8089, "delta": " A_{i,n}$ [C1]. Unlike traditional Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) that operates at"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.347, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 25, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:43.416Z", "t_ms": 8343, "delta": " the activation or sub-network level, MoA operates entirely at the model level via standard prompting and text generation without internal weight changes or"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.468, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 26, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:43.537Z", "t_ms": 8463, "delta": " fine-tuning [C1, C3].\n* **Agent Reuse and Sparsity:** LLMs can be shared or reused within"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.631, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:43.700Z", "t_ms": 8627, "delta": " the same layer or across subsequent layers [C1, C6]. If identical models are used in a single layer, stochastic"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.886, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:43.955Z", "t_ms": 8882, "delta": " temperature sampling allows them to generate diverse responses; this is known as a single-proposer setup where only a sparse subset of distinct"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.073, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:44.142Z", "t_ms": 9069, "delta": " models is active [C1].\n* **Role Consolidation:** Rather than using separate gating and expert networks as in MoE, each LL"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.374, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:44.443Z", "t_ms": 9369, "delta": "M in an MoA layer inherently combines these roles by interpreting prompts and generating refined text [C3].\n\n---\n\n### Combining Layer"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.545, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:44.614Z", "t_ms": 9541, "delta": " Outputs\n\n* **Iterative Generation:** In the initial layer, agents $A_{1,1}, \\dots,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.691, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:44.760Z", "t_ms": 9687, "delta": " A_{1,n}$ independently generate text continuations based on the original user prompt $x_1$ [C"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.898, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:44.967Z", "t_ms": 9894, "delta": "1, C6]. \n* **Aggregate-and-Synthesize Formulation:** For subsequent layers, the intermediate output of layer $i$"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.114, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:45.184Z", "t_ms": 10110, "delta": " ($y_i$) is produced by aggregating the outputs of the current layer's agents along with the original input prompt:\n  $$"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.3, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:45.369Z", "t_ms": 10295, "delta": "y_i = \\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}[A_{i,j}(x_i)] + x_1"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.472, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:45.542Z", "t_ms": 10468, "delta": "$$\n  where $+$ represents text concatenation and $\\oplus$ represents the application of an \"Aggregate-and-Synthesize\""}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.669, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:45.738Z", "t_ms": 10665, "delta": " prompt [C1]. \n* **Prompt Integration:** The Aggregate-and-Synthesize prompt formats all model responses into a numbered"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.011, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:46.080Z", "t_ms": 11007, "delta": " list (e.g., `1. [Model Response from A_{i,1}]`, `2. [Model Response from"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.123, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:46.193Z", "t_ms": 11119, "delta": " A_{i,2}]`, etc.) and instructs the next model to critically evaluate, refine, and synthesize the collective"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.316, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:46.385Z", "t_ms": 11312, "delta": " information into a cohesive, high-quality response [C1].\n* **Final Layer Output:** In practice, intermediate"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.426, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:46.495Z", "t_ms": 11422, "delta": " outputs are passed to the next layer as $x_{i+1} = y_i$ [C1]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.631, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:46.700Z", "t_ms": 11627, "delta": " Because concatenation is not required at the final step, only a single LLM is needed in the final layer ($l$),"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.932, "data": {"request_id": "d34082ea7496", "seq": 43, "ts": "2026-10-28T06:59:47.001Z", "t_ms": 11928, "delta": " and its generated output $A_{l,1}(x_l)$ serves as the ultimate response [C1, C2"}}
